ching, such as searching by aliases or keywords.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Accessibility\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"ComboboxInput has the combobox role with aria-autocomplete, aria-expanded, aria-controls and aria-activedescendant pointing at the highlighted option, so focus stays in the field while screen readers follow the active row. Arrow Down and Arrow Up open the list and move through options, Home and End jump to the ends, Enter selects, and Escape closes and returns focus to the input. ComboboxEmpty uses the status role so a no-results message is announced. With reduced motion enabled, the list opens without the morph and the highlight jumps between rows.\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}],[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"How do I build a searchable select or autocomplete in React?\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"How do I build a searchable select or autocomplete in React?\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-1\",\"children\":\"Compose Combobox with ComboboxTrigger containing ComboboxInput, then ComboboxContent with a ComboboxList of ComboboxItem elements. Add ComboboxEmpty for a no-results message and ComboboxGroup with ComboboxLabel to group options.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Can I customize how options are filtered?\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Can I customize how options are filtered?\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-1\",\"children\":\"Yes. Pass a filter function to Combobox, and give items extra search terms with the keywords prop or a textValue. You can also own the search text with query, defaultQuery and onQueryChange.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Can I control the selected value?\",{\"children\":[